      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "ZD-0892, a neutrophil elastase inhibitor, is under development by AstraZeneca as a potential treatment for chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and peripheral vascular disease (PVD). It is in phase I clinical trials for these two indications [315489]. The compound was originally under investigation for the potential treatment of asthma, but development was discontinued for this indication [266604]. The compound is the follow-up to ZD-8321 (qv) [336599]."},
